## E2. away warns of an Antigravity session, and not of the Claude Code one
$ (the operator, at a terminal) handoff away "carry on"
    away (#2): your go-ahead stands until you run handoff back
    Under it, an item is approved once every reviewer it was sent to approves the same commit; one approval is enough for an item sent to one reviewer. handoff doesn't read your words: to tell the agents something without approving anything, use handoff fyi.
    told implementer and reviewer (#3, #4)
    implementer's session isn't listening now; it gets this the next time it listens.
    reviewer's session isn't listening now; it gets this the next time it listens.
    implementer is an Antigravity session: handoff can wake it 10 times before you type in it.
    handoff: told the operator: Your go-ahead is recorded (#2): carry on Until you run handoff back, items are approved without asking you.
  binding A | role implementer | cli antigravity
  binding R | role reviewer | cli claude

